<!--
  Status-bar notification icon for ALL real Connect notifications (calls, SMS,
  voicemail, missed calls). Android renders the small icon purely from its alpha
  channel as a tinted silhouette, so this MUST be a transparent-background white
  glyph — never a full-colour bitmap. The previous PNG carried an opaque blue
  gradient background, which masked down to a solid blob in the status bar. This
  vector draws only the phone + signal-wave glyph (the Connect mark) in white on
  transparent, so the status bar shows a clean monochrome icon and the shade
  tints it with @color/notification_icon_color.

  The always-on keep-alive foreground-service notification deliberately uses the
  separate fully-transparent ic_keepalive_silent instead, so it shows NO
  status-bar icon at all.
-->
